{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetJbpfSfv3qwVDkbeqWB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses (`ConflictException`, `ResourceNotFoundException`)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler` centrally converts all `ApiException` to `ApiError` envelope with `code`, `message`, `fields`\n- Error codes in `ErrorCode` enum are part of the public API contract\n- `InMemoryShipmentRepository` stores state; tests verify through controller endpoints, not direct repository calls\n- Tests use `MockMvc` with `jsonPath` assertions on response bodies, not just status codes (per the skill guidance)\n- State-changing operations return the new state in response body\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint (unavoidable)\n2. `ApiError.kt` — Must add new `ErrorCode` for invalid status transition (unavoidable—409 requires a distinct code)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for the new endpoint (unavoidable)\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Adding an error code changes the public API contract; must be deliberate\n- Idempotent behavior (repeated confirm succeeds, not fails) is critical for operations\n- State transition from CREATED → CONFIRMED must actually persist\n- Concurrent access to shared `ConcurrentHashMap` must be safe (built in)\n\n**Open questions:**\n\n1. **Which error code should a 409 conflict for an invalid status use?** The enum lacks a status-transition-specific code. Current codes are resource-existence-related. I will add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` as a new code to represent \"cannot confirm from this state.\"\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This covers the case where confirm is attempted on a CANCELLED or invalid-state shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Calls `repository.findById(shipmentId)` to get the shipment\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) if not found\n   - Throws `ConflictException` (409) with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` if status is CANCELLED\n   - If status is CREATED, creates a new shipment with CONFIRMED status and saves it\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns the (updated or unchanged) shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add five new tests:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — verify CREATED → CONFIRMED transition, check response body, then re-read via GET to confirm persistence\n   - `repeated confirm succeeds and changes nothing` — confirm twice, assert second response matches first\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with error code` — write CANCELLED to repo, attempt confirm, assert 409 + error code, re-read via GET to verify state unchanged\n   - `rejects confirming unknown shipment with 404` — confirm non-existent id, assert 404 + SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n   - (Implicit: existing tests remain passing)\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- *Use a generic \"INVALID_STATE\" code* — Rejected because it is imprecise; a client seeing 409 INVALID_STATE cannot distinguish \"confirm failed\" from other state machines. `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` is explicit about what operation was refused.\n- *Reuse SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS* — Rejected; it does not match the failure mode (status is wrong, not that a duplicate was created).\n- *Create the confirm as a service method* — Rejected; the skill and existing endpoints show state-changing logic in the controller, and there is no separate service layer, so no architectural precedent to follow.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Precondition | Call | Repository read | Comparison | Action | Response | Verification |\n|------|--------------|------|-----------------|-----------|--------|----------|---------------|\n| Confirm CREATED | Shipment S-1, status=CREATED | POST /shipments/S-1/confirm | findById(\"S-1\") | status == CREATED | save(s.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | 200, Shipment{status=CONFIRMED} | GET /shipments/S-1 shows CONFIRMED |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED (idempotent) | Shipment S-2, status=CONFIRMED | POST /shipments/S-2/confirm | findById(\"S-2\") | status == CONFIRMED | do nothing | 200, Shipment{status=CONFIRMED} (unchanged) | GET /shipments/S-2 shows CONFIRMED; second confirm matches first response |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | Shipment S-3, status=CANCELLED | POST /shipments/S-3/confirm | findById(\"S-3\") | status == CANCELLED | throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM, ...) | 409 + error envelope | GET /shipments/S-3 shows CANCELLED (unchanged) |\n| Confirm non-existent | No shipment | POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm | findById returns null | n/a | throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...) | 404 + error envelope | — |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirms a created shipment**\n   - Creates S-1 (CREATED)\n   - POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Asserts 200, response body status = CONFIRMED\n   - GET /shipments/S-1 and asserts status = CONFIRMED (proves persistence)\n\n2. **Test: repeated confirm succeeds and changes nothing**\n   - Creates S-2 (CREATED)\n   - POST /shipments/S-2/confirm → response A\n   - POST /shipments/S-2/confirm → response B\n   - Asserts response B status = 200, status = CONFIRMED, matches response A\n\n3. **Test: rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with error code**\n   - Writes S-3 directly to repository with CANCELLED status\n   - POST /shipments/S-3/confirm\n   - Asserts 409, error.code = SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - GET /shipments/S-3 asserts status = CANCELLED (unchanged)\n\n4. **Test: rejects confirming unknown shipment with 404**\n   - POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm\n   - Asserts 404, error.code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n5. **Implicit: existing tests remain passing**\n   - All existing ShipmentControllerTest cases must pass\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1154,"cache_read_input_tokens":18026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1154},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91a988e6-eba9-4b0e-805b-3673b3b90577","uuid":"fd28ebed-2cf0-4d17-ae76-2c66aabb698d","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:02:33.631Z","request_id":"req_011CetJbp4UhHiE83pFXgHGD"}
